1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Could your old school lunch beat meals from nine other countries?

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
Vance brought two friends to settle that question once and for all.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,400
Ten different school lunch trays entered their homemade food showdown.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,900
And these three grown men were taking every bite seriously.

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:17,400
Taste, nutrition, and fullness would decide the winning country.

6
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:20,900
Only one tray could claim the title of school lunch champion.

7
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:24,300
They started with an American tray priced at two fifty.

8
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,800
It had a burger, fries, a donut, and a soda.

9
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:31,300
A donut and soda for lunch? That sparked instant debate.

10
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,800
Nobody could decide if this was lunch or a party.

11
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:38,200
Vance loved the burger and fries more than he expected.

12
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:41,700
Comfort food was clearly winning this first round on taste.

13
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:45,200
Milo and Zack finished their trays and joined the judging.

14
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:48,700
America scored well for flavor, but only four for health.

15
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:52,100
Japan's tray changed the mood as soon as it appeared.

16
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:55,600
Fish, vegetables, and fruit offered a completely different kind of lunch.

17
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:59,100
The guys struggled with chopsticks, then washed everything down with milk.

18
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:02,600
Japan walked away with seventy-one points on their scoreboard.

19
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:06,000
Then India arrived with a price that surprised everyone.

20
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,500
Warm lentils, vegetables, flatbread, and chai filled the colorful tray.

21
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:13,000
They listed this hearty school meal at absolutely no charge.

22
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,500
That alone impressed the judges before Italy even took the stage.

23
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:19,900
Italy's tray looked more like dinner at a family restaurant.

24
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:23,400
Pasta, pizza, salad, and grapes made everyone lean forward.

25
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:26,900
Vance joked that he would never skip school for pizza.

26
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:30,400
He looked ready to give the Italian tray a trophy.

27
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,800
But first, the judges finally finished calculating India's total.

28
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:37,300
India earned fifty points, with fullness helping its score.

29
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:40,800
Italy still looked tempting, but its final score could wait.

30
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:44,300
Now Ukraine brought a comforting, home-style tray to the table.

31
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:47,700
Buckwheat and a savory cutlet were the stars of this meal.

32
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:51,200
Cabbage salad, cheesy bread, and fruit compote rounded it out.

33
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:54,700
It wasn't flashy, but the judges immediately understood its appeal.

34
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:58,200
This was exactly the kind of meal that actually fills you.

35
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:01,600
All three plates were cleared before anyone could say another word.

36
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:05,100
Ukraine surged into the lead with seventy-five total points.

37
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:08,600
Mexico arrived next, bringing an entirely different lunchtime energy.

38
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:12,100
The tray paired a casserole with a generously filled taco.

39
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:15,600
Chips, guacamole, and chocolate milk made the deal even sweeter.

40
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:19,100
And the listed price was just one dollar for everything.

41
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:22,600
Vance gave the flavor a perfect ten without hesitation.

42
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:26,100
But nutrition pulled Mexico's overall score down to sixty.

43
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:29,600
Brazil answered with one of the freshest looking trays yet.

44
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:33,100
Seasoned grains, a green wrap, fruit, and mango juice stood out.

45
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:36,600
That huge green wrap almost looked bigger than a textbook.

46
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:40,100
The judges needed both hands just to hold each bite.

47
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:43,600
Brazil scored a perfect thirty for their health category.

48
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:47,100
That pushed its total to seventy-five, tying Ukraine.

49
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:50,600
Next, China's colorful tray gave the judges even more choices.

50
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:54,100
Rice, savory meat, and dumplings immediately caught everyone's attention.

51
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:57,600
Braised greens, an egg, and orange slices completed the spread.

52
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:01,100
Suddenly, this felt more like a weekend feast than school lunch.

53
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:04,600
Their chopstick skills were shaky, but the dumplings disappeared fast.

54
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:08,100
China collected sixty-nine points after everyone finished eating.

55
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:11,600
Spain was next with a colorful Mediterranean-inspired lunch tray.

56
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:15,100
Rice, cucumber salad, and fruit gave the meal a fresh look.

57
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:18,600
That little foil drink pouch brought back everyone's childhood memories.

58
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:22,100
Even the judges were smiling before the final scores appeared.

59
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:25,600
Spain took the lead with an impressive seventy-six points.

60
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:29,100
Only Turkey's tray and Italy's final score were still waiting.

61
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:32,600
Turkey served up a lunch that looked restaurant-worthy.

62
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:36,100
Grilled kebab, fresh herbs, and flatbread covered the tray.

63
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:39,600
Then baklava arrived, making dessert feel like a bonus round.

64
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:43,100
But the salted yogurt drink caught all three judges off guard.

65
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:46,600
The grilled food earned praise, while that drink divided opinions.

66
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:50,100
Nobody expected their first sip to taste quite that salty.

67
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:53,600
A perfect fullness score still gave Turkey sixty-two points overall.

68
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,100
And at last, everyone turned toward Italy's waiting scorecard.

69
00:03:57,100 --> 00:04:00,600
Its judges loved the combination of taste, nutrition, and satisfaction.

70
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:04,100
Italy won their challenge with a massive eighty-six points.

71
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:07,600
Apparently, a plate of pasta can make school seem exciting.

72
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:11,050
At least that's what these three very hungry judges decided.

